'' TKO0936, fbc's 17 (T38): a word between 'declare' and the procedure keyword that is not
'' a modifier -- 'explicit', which fbc does not have, or any other -- is refused. tiko took
'' it as the procedure keyword and accepted 'declare explicit constructor', so the implicit
'' conversion the writer meant to switch off still happened. 'const' and 'static' are
'' modifiers and are fine. Lines identical to fbc-modern's errors. See
'' DeclareProcKeyword_ in parser/declparam.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/declare-stray-word.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare-stray-word.bas(3,13): error TKO0936
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare-stray-word.bas(4,13): error TKO0936
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 2
